 "applies_to": "PRO1-Mod of the PRO1 series (PRO1-S/-2T/-Mb/-Mod), register map of user manual version 302 (2025).",
 "summary": "The PRO1-Mod is inepro's single-phase MID DIN-rail energy meter with an RS485 Modbus RTU port (this is the older PRO line, not the 2026 PRO1/PRO2 template). Every measurement is an IEEE 754 float, high word first, read with function 03 from hex blocks 4000h (setup), 5000h (live values) and 6000h (energy). The map covers voltage, current, power, power factor, frequency, total/tariff energy and the writable ID, baud, parity, S0, tariff and combination-code settings.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "The map prints hex addresses that go into the request unchanged; the manual's example frames are 01 06 4003 000A (set Modbus ID) and 01 06 6048 0002 (set tariff). So 5012h (total active power) is wire address 20498. Do not enter the hex numbers as decimal."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "PRO1 Series MID/MIR Single phase energy meter - User manual",
  "doc_number": "Version 302",
  "revision_date": "2025",
  "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6617f74190bf0a53bfd776e8/6ac4ef8c621e952209fa3278_PRO1%20user%20manual%20V302.pdf",
  "pages": "Program modes and combination code pp. 13-15; Modbus ID/baud/parity p. 15-16; Appendix 3 Modbus (A3.1 p. 24, register map and write commands pp. 25-26)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "The PDF is inepro's own user manual (hosted on inepro's website CDN).",
  "The register map is shared with the PRO380; rows marked '*PRO380 only' (L2/L3 values, per-phase energy, CT ratio/mode, L2/L3 current direction and quadrants) are left out of this single-phase file.",
  "'Float ABCD' = IEEE 754 32-bit float, high word first. 'Signed' rows are 16-bit integers.",
  "Units are as printed: power in kW, kvar and kVA (not W), energy in kWh and kvarh.",
  "Left out: serial number, meter code, checksum and active status word (typed HEX with no decoding), LCD cycle time (HEX; the write example 0025 for 25 s suggests BCD), current direction (ASCII) and error code 4015h (no code list given).",
  "Baud rate (4004h) is written as the plain number, e.g. 2580h = 9600. The Modbus section allows 1200, 2400, 4800 and 9600.",
  "Combination code 11 is marked PRO380 only and is left out of the value list.",
  "The day-counter write row prints function 06 and length 1, but its example frame writes 2 registers with function 16; it is listed here as a 2-register float."
 ],
